          "rendered_stream": "virtual_stereo_center_rgb",
          "reason": "The DROID sim proxy uses a laterally offset ZED Mini left eye with a Robotiq 2F-85, while AXIS renders native Panda geometry. The rendered pinhole is first moved to a virtual stereo-center proxy: in the validated reference replay pose, this moves the fingertip midpoint from u/W=0.680 to u/W=0.507. A subsequent +8 degree local pitch was selected from fixed-plus-four-randomized render comparisons because it exposes substantially more of both Panda fingers without introducing the broad palm occlusion seen in stronger translation-plus-rotation candidates. Camera position, depth, and FOV remain unchanged by the pitch override. This is not derived from gripper width and is not a claim that arbitrary distant workspace points remain centered across robot motion."
